# Our tuned settings for Mario Kart World on this machine (RTX 3060, 12 GB,
# Ryzen 7 3700X). Every value here is a knob of adriadam10/mkw-recomp, so the
# upstream can be updated without touching this file.
#
# Measured on a 24-kart race (the attract demo's), median frame over thousands
# of race frames. See docs/PERFORMANCE.md.

# The game copy. Point these at your own dump: a folder with exefs/ and romfs/,
# or a .nup/.nx the port can read.
MKW_DUMP=${MKW_DUMP:-/mnt/Data/mkw-dump}
# Where the game is installed for the port: the prepared SPIR-V, the pipeline
# cache and the settings live here (the port looks for them in the game dir, and
# NOT next to the binary - that is what makes the pipeline prewarm work).
MKW_GAME_DIR=${MKW_GAME_DIR:-}

# The mouse: MKW_MOUSE_SENS=0 turns the mouse camera off, and with it SDL's
# relative mouse mode, so the game never grabs and hides the pointer. The
# upstream's default is 1, which does grab it.
MKW_MOUSE_SENS=${MKW_MOUSE_SENS:-0}

# Internal resolution. 720 lines (1280x720) is the upstream's race-run default;
# the race frame is a serial chain (game -> recording -> GPU -> completion) and
# the GPU's share sits on it, so 540 lines (960x540) is worth +27% of the race's
# frame rate here (30 -> 47 fps median). 480 lines holds a locked 16.667 ms
# (60 fps) in the race's lighter stretches. 720 for the sharper picture.
MKW_RESOLUTION=${MKW_RESOLUTION:-540}

# The memory mirror: pools at most this many 2 MiB regions apart share one
# query, so the frame does fewer GPU round trips (it was doing ~106 a frame).
# +19% on its own.
MKW_MIRROR_GAP=${MKW_MIRROR_GAP:-8}

# No 256-draw serial head before the recording's chunks: the chunks are handed
# out as the walk goes, so the GPU can start earlier. +11% on its own.
MKW_REPLAY_PAR_HEAD=${MKW_REPLAY_PAR_HEAD:-0}

# Build every pipeline the key file knows before the game starts, so a race
# does not stall on a pipeline build. The upstream's default.
MKW_PIPE_PREBUILD=${MKW_PIPE_PREBUILD:-1}

# The frame rate: the console's own "Automatic" picks 60 or 30 frame by frame,
# so a race reads as a mixture of the two and still runs at real speed.
# MKW_FPS=60 pins it to 60 (the console's "Fixed 60"), but then the game holds
# 60 Hz and runs in SLOW MOTION if the machine cannot keep up - worse here.
MKW_FPS=${MKW_FPS:-auto}

# DO NOT trim the textures on a 12 GB card: MKW_TEX_MAX=1024 and
# MKW_TEX_QUALITY=half black the road out completely in a race (the track
# renders with no surface at all). They exist to fit a smaller card. The race
# uses 8.3 GB of the 10.4 GB heap limit with them off.
MKW_TEX_MAX=${MKW_TEX_MAX:-0}
MKW_TEX_QUALITY=${MKW_TEX_QUALITY:-full}

# The GPU's own heap: the driver reports a budget and the port stops
# MKW_VRAM_MARGIN (300 MiB) below it. Raise the margin if the other GPU apps
# on the desktop are holding VRAM (ZBrush takes ~2 GB and shrinks the budget).
MKW_VRAM_MARGIN=${MKW_VRAM_MARGIN:-300}
